invariant: INV-36
file: build.zig
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: build.zig takes a WIDEMUL value for a host object, which the Makefile
  refuses, so the two builds stop refusing the same values, and
  WIDEMUL=native writes -DCH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL beside -DCH_CPU_RUNTIME for
  ct.h to stop. test/widemul-builds.sh requires zig build to refuse
  WIDEMUL=native and WIDEMUL=decomposed for a host object.

--- old
    if (config.widemul) |widemul| {
        std.process.fatal("WIDEMUL={t} chooses a device object's multiply, and TRUST={t} ROLE={t} " ++ builds ++
            "holds both multiplies and picks one per session from ch_cfg.cpu " ++
            "(docs/decisions.md 89): drop WIDEMUL" ++ device, .{ widemul, config.trust, config.role });
    }
--- new
